{"reference":"2 Chronicles 33","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":33,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Manasseh’s Humbling and Return","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 10–17 present Manasseh’s reversal as a defining movement in the account: after ignoring warning, he is brought into distress, humbles himself, prays, returns to Jerusalem, recognizes the LORD, and removes the foreign worship he had established. This sequence belongs to a recurring pattern in Judah’s royal narratives in which seeking the LORD, humility, prayer, and turning away from prior wrongdoing are set alongside the response to prophetic instruction.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 33:10-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_033_c9a9d1ed789e56d8aea63be4"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}